## STEP 2: CREATE THE WIN-RATE TRACKER SPREADSHEET (15 min)

This is the "living document" feature that makes v3.0 different from static templates.

**Create a Google Sheet:**

| Column | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| A: Date | When you sent the proposal |
| B: Client Name | Who you sent it to |
| C: Platform | Fiverr / Upwork / Direct / Other |
| D: Project Type | What kind of work |
| E: Price Quoted | What you asked for |
| F: Outcome | Hired / Rejected / No Response |
| G: Confidence Score | 1-10 from Polish Prompt |
| H: Revenue Anchor | What you calculated |
| I: Authority Gap | Strong / Weak / None |
| J: New Rule Extracted | From Learn Route Input |
| K: Notes | What you learned |

**Add these formulas:**
- Win rate: `=COUNTIF(F:F,"Hired")/COUNTA(F:F)` (format as percentage)
- Average confidence score: `=AVERAGE(G:G)`
- Total revenue from hires: `=SUMIF(F:F,"Hired",E:E)`

**Share the sheet:** "Anyone with the link can view" — buyers see your live win rate.

**File name:** `proposal-forge-tracker-template.xlsx`

